# Qandyagash Life Backend

This backend is a lightweight Express API for a city services platform.

## Features

- Auth mock login
- Taxi orders
- Food orders
- Delivery orders
- Payment initialization and confirmation
- In-memory storage for demo/testing

## Quick start

```bash
cd backend
npm install
cp .env.example .env
npm run dev
```

## Base URL

```text
http://localhost:4000
```

## Endpoints

### Health
- GET /api/health

### Auth
- POST /api/auth/login

### Orders
- POST /api/orders/taxi
- POST /api/orders/food
- POST /api/orders/delivery
- GET /api/orders

### Payments
- POST /api/payments/create
- POST /api/payments/confirm
- GET /api/payments

## Payment providers

The current implementation supports a mock provider and is ready to integrate with Kaspi or Halyk by replacing the mock logic in the route handlers.

## Notes

This is a demo backend for startup MVP and can be replaced with Postgres + Prisma or NestJS for production.

## Example request body

```json
{
  "userId": "123",
  "amount": 3500,
  "currency": "KZT",
  "provider": "Kaspi"
}
```

## Production recommendations

- Add real authentication with JWT or Firebase Auth
- Store data in PostgreSQL
- Add provider SDK integration for Kaspi/Halyk
- Add Stripe or local gateway support
- Implement Redis for caching and rate limiting


